# PHD-MAIN-FILL-v1 CDGS variant: the one change beyond adapter v2 (order 5.1 2-4, user decision 10-15; a reproduction variant, order 5.1 5).
# cdgs-release-adapters-v2 (SB/sources, PHD-MAIN-BASELINES-v1) -> cdgs-release-adapters-v3 (SL/sources). Only scene/dataset_readers.py.
# Switched on per scene by "alignment": "identity" in jbgs_cdgs_options.json; without that line adapter v3 runs exactly as v2
# (checked: SL/prep/cdgs/same_supervision_B0_b10_LoD2.json, switch_off_equals_v2).
# With the switch: the per-view fit (optimize_depth's Adam) is skipped, scale 1 and shift 0; the alignment loss is computed in place by
# jbgs_identity_depth with optimize_depth's own lines (the view's own observed SfM points, the same reprojection-error weights and their
# max-normalisation, the same 0.1 % prune, both depths divided by the site's s as v2, the negative-depth term 0); the depth weight
# 0.6 exp(-150 L_align) is the official line; the supervision depth and the confidence map are made from the prior render depth in
# metres as read. Each view's record in jbgs_alignment.json gets the v2 official values of the same view beside ("v2_reference").
